  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 8, P = 15. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[9, 0, 12, 5, 5, 4, 6, 3], [12, 7, 14, 13, 14, 5, 10, 0], [8, 9, 0, 13, 11, 8, 8, 10]], sigma = [6, 4, 5, 7, 1, 2, 0, 3], B = [11, 7, 13, 12, 7, 13, 11, 12].",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data"
  ],
  "date": "2026",
  "novelty": "known_parameters",
  "notes": "Literature baseline: a reproduction of a code published with arXiv:2609.30069, rebuilt from the authors' data repository (https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data/blob/306b31d/codes/reverse_fold/j3l8/specs/reverse_j3l8_p15_k17.json). Not a new construction. The authors report d = 6 as exact. Their lower-bound search output is not in the repository, so this entry carries an upper bound backed by their weight-6 Pauli logical, stored as the witness."
